MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

YG-9. Full create/update/delete for events, show slots and ticket tiers.

Event forms send exactly what EventRequestDto accepts, with type required —
a missing type is a 400. Ticket-tier forms send { name, price, totalQty } only;
availableQty is server-managed and shown read-only.

Shows and tiers are read per parent (the API has no bulk list), so these pages
fan out: events, then shows per event, then tiers per show. That is a handful of
parallel requests at demo scale, and the event/show filters keep it bounded. If
the catalogue grows, the fix is a bulk admin endpoint rather than more fan-out.

The dashboard derives every figure from the live catalogue — seats sold is the
sum of totalQty minus availableQty, revenue is that times tier price. The mock
version's booking count and recent-bookings table are gone: there is no admin
endpoint that lists bookings (/api/bookings/me is caller-scoped), so rather
than invent numbers the panel says what is missing and why.
